3.5.0 audit performance and equivalence report
Actual local OpenCV processing. Screen capture, Windows focus, network and Roblox rendering are excluded.
PASS identical slot geometry, selection and card types on 32 fixture variants: selected/unselected, scaled, blurred, covered and blank.
Warm median snapshot (7 batches of 150), version 3.4.0: 1.710 ms; version 3.5.0 with artwork/label validation: 1.766 ms.
Change: +3.2%. The new validation has a cost; this is not a claim of faster image processing.
Primary responsiveness change: missing-plan mutation OCR now runs outside the foreground action worker, with at most two outstanding scans.
The audit test holds an OCR result pending through 100 polls: zero extra focus calls and one submitted scan; a peer equips before the result finishes.
The 100000-message UI stress stays within the configured mailbox limit; the two-worker executor rejects 1000 excess submissions without queue growth.
See VALIDATION_3_5.log for detector, input and Qt results. No live Roblox acceptance, overnight reliability or packaged Windows install was tested.
